<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>SOC Analyst Lab: Questions, Hints and Final Answers</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: Calibri, 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; color: #1e293b; margin: 35px; }
    h1 { color: #0f172a; font-size: 22pt; border-bottom: 2px solid #0f172a; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-bottom: 4px; }
    .subtitle { color: #64748b; font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 25px; }
    h2 { color: #047857; font-size: 15pt; border-bottom: 1px solid #cbd5e1; padding-bottom: 4px; margin-top: 30px; }
    .q-card { border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 6px; padding: 14px; margin-bottom: 20px; background: #ffffff; }
    .q-title { font-weight: bold; color: #0f172a; font-size: 11.5pt; margin-bottom: 10px; }
    .hint-box { background: #fffbeb; border-left: 4px solid #f59e0b; padding: 8px 12px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-size: 10pt; color: #92400e; }
    .ans-box { background: #f0fdf4; border-left: 4px solid #16a34a; padding: 8px 12px; font-size: 10.5pt; color: #166534; }
    code { font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 2px 5px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 10pt; color: #b91c1c; font-weight: bold; }
    table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px; }
    th { background: #0f172a; color: white; padding: 8px 10px; text-align: left; font-size: 10pt; }
    td { border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; padding: 8px 10px; font-size: 10pt; }
    .walkthrough-step { background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
    .walkthrough-step strong { color: #0369a1; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <h1>🛡️ SOC Analyst Lab: Web Attack Forensics & IoC Hunting</h1>
  <p class="subtitle"><strong>Official Lab Guide, Question Bank & Master Answer Key</strong></p>

  <p><em>This document contains the step-by-step walkthrough to perform the three attacks (SQL Injection, Directory Traversal, and Cross-Site Scripting), followed by the 8 official investigation questions with hints and final answers for your assessment platform.</em></p>

  <hr>

  <h2>Part 1: How to Perform the Lab</h2>
  
  <div class="walkthrough-step">
    <strong>Attack 1: SQL Injection (SQLi)</strong><br>
    1. Open the <strong>Target Application</strong> tab and navigate to <strong>"🏢 Asset Directory"</strong>.<br>
    2. Test for error-based vulnerability by entering a single quote: <code>'</code>. Notice the application returns an unhandled <code>HTTP 500 Internal Server Error</code> revealing PostgreSQL syntax details.<br>
    3. Perform data exfiltration using a UNION query:
       <br><code>' UNION SELECT 1,username,password_hash,email,role FROM users--</code><br>
    4. The leaked database table displays the admin secret key: <code>BLITZ{5ql1_3xf1ltr4t10n_k9x27p4}</code>.<br>
    5. Switch to the <strong>SOC SIEM Console</strong>, filter by <code>status:500</code> or <code>category:sqli</code>, and click <strong>"Inspect"</strong> to analyze the logged query parameters.
  </div>

  <div class="walkthrough-step">
    <strong>Attack 2: Directory Traversal (Path Traversal / LFI)</strong><br>
    1. In the <strong>Target Application</strong>, navigate to <strong>"📁 Document Center"</strong>.<br>
    2. The application fetches files via <code>/api/documents?file=...</code>.<br>
    3. Test escaping the document root to access the internal system secrets file:
       <br><code>../../../../system/secrets.env</code><br>
    4. The server returns the configuration file exposing Flag: <code>BLITZ{p4th_tr4v3rs4l_f1l3_r34d_8a3d1}</code>.<br>
    5. Switch to the <strong>SOC SIEM Console</strong>, filter by <code>category:path_traversal</code> or <code>rule:RULE-SEC-006</code>, and inspect the raw dot-dot-slash (<code>../</code>) path traversal sequences.
  </div>

  <div class="walkthrough-step">
    <strong>Attack 3: Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)</strong><br>
    1. In the <strong>Target Application</strong>, go to <strong>"Asset Directory"</strong> (Reflected XSS) or <strong>"Support"</strong> (Stored XSS).<br>
    2. Submit an executable script payload:
       <br><code>&lt;script&gt;alert('XSS')&lt;/script&gt;</code><br>
    3. The browser security sandbox executes the script and reveals Flag: <code>BLITZ{x55_d0m_3x3cut10n_9c417e2}</code>.<br>
    4. In the <strong>SOC SIEM Console</strong>, filter by <code>category:xss</code> and inspect the raw URL percent encoding <code>%3C</code> for the opening script bracket.
  </div>

  <hr>

  <h2>Part 2: Official Questions, Hints & Final Answers</h2>

  <!-- Question 1 -->
  <div class="q-card">
    <div class="q-title">Question 1 (SQL Injection Execution)</div>
    <p>Perform a SQL injection attack in the Asset Directory search bar using a UNION-based query to exfiltrate the hidden <code>users</code> table. What is the administrative secret flag retrieved from the database?</p>
    <div class="hint-box">
      <strong>💡 Hint:</strong> In the Asset Directory search bar, enter <code>' UNION SELECT 1,username,password_hash,email,role FROM users--</code> and inspect the leaked administrator record.
    </div>
    <div class="ans-box">
      <strong>🎯 Final Answer:</strong> <code>BLITZ{5ql1_3xf1ltr4t10n_k9x27p4}</code>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Question 2 -->
  <div class="q-card">
    <div class="q-title">Question 2 (SQL Injection Web Log Forensics)</div>
    <p>When testing input fields for unhandled SQL injection, an unescaped single quote character (<code>'</code>) caused the backend database to throw a syntax exception. What HTTP response status code was returned by the server and recorded in the SIEM access logs?</p>
    <div class="hint-box">
      <strong>💡 Hint:</strong> Filter the SIEM console for server error status codes in the 5xx range or inspect the log entry generated after submitting an isolated quote <code>'</code>.
    </div>
    <div class="ans-box">
      <strong>🎯 Final Answer:</strong> <code>500</code> <em>(also accept: 500 Internal Server Error)</em>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Question 3 -->
  <div class="q-card">
    <div class="q-title">Question 3 (Directory Traversal Execution)</div>
    <p>Exploit the Document Center endpoint (<code>/api/documents</code>) using Directory Traversal path escape sequences to read the protected server configuration file (<code>/system/secrets.env</code>). What secret flag is exposed inside?</p>
    <div class="hint-box">
      <strong>💡 Hint:</strong> Enter <code>../../../../system/secrets.env</code> into the Document Center file input to traverse up from the storage root.
    </div>
    <div class="ans-box">
      <strong>🎯 Final Answer:</strong> <code>BLITZ{p4th_tr4v3rs4l_f1l3_r34d_8a3d1}</code>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Question 4 -->
  <div class="q-card">
    <div class="q-title">Question 4 (Directory Traversal Web Log Forensics)</div>
    <p>Inspect the raw URI parameters recorded in the SIEM for your directory traversal request. What standard two-character dot sequence followed by a forward slash is repeated to escape the web document root?</p>
    <div class="hint-box">
      <strong>💡 Hint:</strong> In Unix/Linux file system paths, what notation represents traversing to the parent directory?
    </div>
    <div class="ans-box">
      <strong>🎯 Final Answer:</strong> <code>../</code> <em>(also accept: ..%2f, ..%2F)</em>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Question 5 -->
  <div class="q-card">
    <div class="q-title">Question 5 (Cross-Site Scripting Execution)</div>
    <p>Inject an XSS payload into the application (via the search bar or support ticket form) that executes JavaScript in the browser context. What challenge flag is displayed upon successful script execution?</p>
    <div class="hint-box">
      <strong>💡 Hint:</strong> Enter <code>&lt;script&gt;alert('XSS')&lt;/script&gt;</code> into the search bar or support ticket description and inspect the sandbox execution pop-up.
    </div>
    <div class="ans-box">
      <strong>🎯 Final Answer:</strong> <code>BLITZ{x55_d0m_3x3cut10n_9c417e2}</code>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Question 6 -->
  <div class="q-card">
    <div class="q-title">Question 6 (Cross-Site Scripting Web Log Forensics)</div>
    <p>In the raw web access logs, web browsers automatically URL-encode special characters. What is the two-character hexadecimal URL percent-encoding for the opening tag bracket (<code>&lt;</code>) in the logged XSS request URI?</p>
    <div class="hint-box">
      <strong>💡 Hint:</strong> Look at the raw request URI in the SIEM log inspector for the <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> tag. In ASCII, character 60 converts to hex 3C.
    </div>
    <div class="ans-box">
      <strong>🎯 Final Answer:</strong> <code>%3C</code> <em>(also accept: %3c)</em>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Question 7 -->
  <div class="q-card">
    <div class="q-title">Question 7 (Threat Actor IP Identification)</div>
    <p>Analyze the historical baseline telemetry in the SIEM console. What external source IP address conducted directory traversal reconnaissance by probing the Unix user file <code>/etc/passwd</code>?</p>
    <div class="hint-box">
      <strong>💡 Hint:</strong> In the SIEM console, search for <code>passwd</code> or <code>rule:RULE-SEC-006</code> and check the Client IP column.
    </div>
    <div class="ans-box">
      <strong>🎯 Final Answer:</strong> <code>198.51.100.88</code>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Question 8 -->
  <div class="q-card">
    <div class="q-title">Question 8 (Security Remediation)</div>
    <p>What secure coding defense mechanism should be implemented in application source code to completely prevent SQL injection vulnerabilities by separating SQL query structure from user-supplied input data?</p>
    <div class="hint-box">
      <strong>💡 Hint:</strong> It involves pre-compiling the query and binding input variables separately.
    </div>
    <div class="ans-box">
      <strong>🎯 Final Answer:</strong> <code>parameterized queries</code> <em>(also accept: prepared statements, parameterization)</em>
    </div>
  </div>

  <hr>

  <h2>Part 3: Master Flags Cheat Sheet</h2>
  <table>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 25%;">Attack Vector</th>
      <th style="width: 35%;">Trigger Location</th>
      <th style="width: 40%;">Final Flag</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>SQL Injection</strong></td>
      <td>Asset Directory Search (<code>UNION SELECT</code>)</td>
      <td><code>BLITZ{5ql1_3xf1ltr4t10n_k9x27p4}</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Directory Traversal</strong></td>
      <td>Document Center (<code>/system/secrets.env</code>)</td>
      <td><code>BLITZ{p4th_tr4v3rs4l_f1l3_r34d_8a3d1}</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Cross-Site Scripting</strong></td>
      <td>Search / Support Ticket (<code>&lt;script&gt;</code>)</td>
      <td><code>BLITZ{x55_d0m_3x3cut10n_9c417e2}</code></td>
    </tr>
  </table>

</body>
</html>
